WEBVTT

00:00:11.813 --> 00:00:13.903
I miss you.

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:17.123
Lovely.

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:19.430
All she wants to do is snog me.

00:00:19.473 --> 00:00:20.910
My lips are getting chapped.
Look.

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:22.955
I'll take your word for it.

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:35.359
So, what happens to you?

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:38.405
What happens if you break
an Unbreakable Vow?

00:00:38.449 --> 00:00:40.277
You die.

00:00:44.542 --> 00:00:46.761
WOMAN:
Wait, the pudding's still here.

00:00:47.893 --> 00:00:49.155
REMUS:
Voldemort has chosen

00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:51.244
Draco Malfoy for a mission?

00:00:51.288 --> 00:00:52.637
I know it sounds mad.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.204
Has it occurred to you,
Harry, that Snape

00:00:54.247 --> 00:00:56.467
was simply pretending
to offer Draco help

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.817
so he could find out
what he was up to?

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.166
That's not what it sounded like.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.081
NYMPHADORA:
Perhaps Harry's right, Remus.

00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:04.083
To make an Unbreakable Vow,
it's--

00:01:04.127 --> 00:01:06.868
It comes down to whether or not
you trust Dumbledore's judgment.

00:01:06.912 --> 00:01:10.263
Dumbledore trusts Snape,
therefore I do.

00:01:10.307 --> 00:01:12.439
Dumbledore can make mistakes,
he said so himself.

00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:13.527
You're blinded by hatred.

00:01:13.571 --> 00:01:15.747
I'm not.
Yes, you are.

00:01:17.357 --> 00:01:20.491
People are disappearing,
Harry, daily.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:22.623
We can only place our trust
in a handful of people.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:25.757
If we start fighting
amongst ourselves, we're doomed.

00:01:29.152 --> 00:01:31.458
MOLLY:Ginny?

00:01:45.342 --> 00:01:47.083
[CLEARS THROAT]

00:01:50.086 --> 00:01:51.783
Open up, you.

00:01:53.306 --> 00:01:55.091
Don't you trust me?

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.402
It's good.

00:02:02.446 --> 00:02:05.144
RON:
Yeah, I'll just-- Get-- Yeah.

00:02:12.804 --> 00:02:13.848
Pie?

00:02:13.892 --> 00:02:15.894
Not for me, no.

00:02:20.986 --> 00:02:23.336
Mm.

00:02:27.427 --> 00:02:29.125
ARTHUR:
You'll have to forgive Remus.

00:02:29.168 --> 00:02:33.042
It takes its toll,
his condition.

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:35.218
HARRY:
Are you all right, Mr. Weasley?

00:02:35.261 --> 00:02:37.959
We're being followed, all of us.

00:02:38.003 --> 00:02:41.267
Most days,
Molly doesn't leave the house.

00:02:41.311 --> 00:02:43.530
It's not been easy.

00:02:45.402 --> 00:02:46.968
Did you get my owl?

00:02:47.012 --> 00:02:49.188
Yes, I did.

00:02:50.581 --> 00:02:51.712
If Dumbledore's traveling,

00:02:51.756 --> 00:02:53.758
then that's news
to the Ministry,

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:56.935
but perhaps that's the way
Dumbledore wants it.

00:02:56.978 --> 00:03:00.069
As for Draco Malfoy,

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:01.374
I know a bit more.

00:03:01.418 --> 00:03:03.072
Go on.

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:05.074
I sent an agent
to Borgin and Burkes.

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:07.554
I think,
from what you described,

00:03:07.598 --> 00:03:09.382
what you and Ron saw
at the end of the summer,

00:03:09.426 --> 00:03:13.082
the object that Draco
is so interested in

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.735
is a vanishing cabinet.

00:03:14.779 --> 00:03:16.911
A vanishing cabinet?

00:03:16.955 --> 00:03:21.090
They were all the rage when
Voldemort first rose to power.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.613
You can see the appeal.

00:03:22.656 --> 00:03:24.397
Should Death Eaters
come knocking,

00:03:24.441 --> 00:03:27.096
one simply had to slip inside

00:03:27.139 --> 00:03:29.576
and disappear
for an hour or two.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.491
They can transport you anywhere.

00:03:31.535 --> 00:03:35.060
Tricky contraptions though,
very temperamental.

00:03:35.104 --> 00:03:38.150
What happened to it?
The one at Borgin and Burkes?

00:03:38.194 --> 00:03:39.412
Nothing.

00:03:39.456 --> 00:03:42.372
It's still there.

00:03:51.903 --> 00:03:53.861
NYMPHADORA:
It was delicious, Molly, really.

00:03:53.905 --> 00:03:55.341
MOLLY:
Are you sure you won't stay?

00:03:55.385 --> 00:03:57.778
No, we should go.

00:03:57.822 --> 00:04:00.825
The first night of the cycle's
always the worst.

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:02.870
Remus?

00:04:10.835 --> 00:04:12.837
Sweetheart.

00:04:15.231 --> 00:04:16.580
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

00:04:20.671 --> 00:04:22.542
Has Ron gone to bed?

00:04:22.586 --> 00:04:25.545
Um... Not yet. No.

00:04:27.243 --> 00:04:28.679
Shoelace.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:43.172
Merry Christmas, Harry.

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:46.131
Merry Christmas.

00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:47.959
[WHOOSHING]

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:53.225
[♪♪♪]

00:05:00.537 --> 00:05:02.365
[CACKLES]

00:05:03.279 --> 00:05:05.672
Harry, no!
Remus!

00:05:15.029 --> 00:05:16.030
Ginny!

00:05:19.817 --> 00:05:24.125
BELLATRIX:
I killed Sirius Black!
I killed Sirius Black!

00:05:24.169 --> 00:05:27.172
You coming to get me?

00:05:27.216 --> 00:05:28.652
[CACKLING]

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:31.611
Harry, can you get me?
You coming to get me?

00:05:37.095 --> 00:05:40.490
[PANTING]

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.860
Harry?

00:06:02.903 --> 00:06:05.384
[LOW GROWLING]

00:06:20.138 --> 00:06:22.096
Stupefy!

